<w:document xmlns:wpc="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingCanvas" xmlns:mo="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/mac/office/2008/main" xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006" xmlns:mv="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:mac:vml" xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" xmlns:m="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/math" xmlns:v="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml" xmlns:wp14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingDrawing" xmlns:wp="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/wordprocessingDrawing" xmlns:w10="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main" xmlns:w14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordml" xmlns:wpg="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingGroup" xmlns:wpi="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingInk" xmlns:wne="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2006/wordml" xmlns:wps="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingShape" mc:Ignorable="w14 wp14"><w:body><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Title"/><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>Tri-County Commercial Loan Portfolio Review</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>Q4 2025  |  Prepared by Credit Review Department</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p/><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading1"/><w:spacing w:before="240" w:after="80"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>1. Executive Summary</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="80"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>This report presents the results of the Q4 2025 quarterly review of the Tri-County commercial loan portfolio, conducted in accordance with the Loan Portfolio Review Policy. The portfolio comprises 29 active commercial loans with an aggregate outstanding balance of $134,656,509 as of the review date.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="80"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>The review identified nine individual covenant breaches distributed across six affected loans, three Watch List designations driven by risk-rating criteria, one non-performing loan currently in Chapter 11 bankruptcy proceedings, three concentration-limit exceedances, and eleven open exceptions requiring active monitoring or legal coordination. The overall portfolio carries elevated risk due to the concentration of adversely rated exposure in a single non-performing credit (LN-008) and structural over-concentration in commercial mortgage loan types and a single loan-officer relationship.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading1"/><w:spacing w:before="240" w:after="80"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>2. Portfolio Overview</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="80"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>The portfolio includes 29 loans originated between 2020 and 2023, spanning industries including commercial real estate, manufacturing, retail, hospitality, healthcare, technology, food distribution, and energy. Collateral types range from commercial mortgages and equipment to accounts receivable and vehicle inventories.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="80"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>Loan type distribution:</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:tbl><w:tblPr><w:tblStyle w:val="TableGrid"/><w:tblW w:type="auto" w:w="0"/><w:tblLook w:firstColumn="1" w:firstRow="1" w:lastColumn="0" w:lastRow="0" w:noHBand="0" w:noVBand="1" w:val="04A0"/></w:tblPr><w:tblGrid><w:gridCol w:w="2160"/><w:gridCol w:w="2160"/><w:gridCol w:w="2160"/><w:gridCol w:w="2160"/></w:tblGrid><w:tr><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:type="dxa" w:w="2160"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:r><w:rPr><w:b/></w:rPr><w:t>Loan Type</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:type="dxa" w:w="2160"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:r><w:rPr><w:b/></w:rPr><w:t>Loan Count</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:type="dxa" w:w="2160"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:r><w:rPr><w:b/></w:rPr><w:t>Aggregate Balance ($)</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:type="dxa